p the two off‑diagonal rectangles are\nfilled with a single tile, and the process continues inside the two diagonal\nblocks.  The total number of tiles produced is exactly \\(2034\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 4.   Conclusion  \n\nThe lower bound (3) shows that no tiling can use fewer than \\(2034\\) tiles,\nand the recursive construction described in § 3 attains this number.\nTherefore the minimum possible number of rectangular tiles that Matilda must\nplace is  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2034}.\n\\]"
