this construction uses exactly\n\n\\[\n2(n-1)=2\\cdot2024=4048\n\\]\n\ntiles.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 6.  Minimality  \n\nThe construction uses \\(2(n-1)\\) tiles, while (3) shows that no tiling can use fewer.  Therefore the number \\(2(n-1)\\) is the minimum possible.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 7.  Answer for the given board  \n\nFor the \\(2025\\times2025\\) board (\\(n=2025\\)) the minimum number of tiles is  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4048}.\n\\]"
