belonging to\ndifferent columns are also disjoint because they occupy different\ncolumns.  Consequently the collection  \n\n\\[\n\\{R_j^{\\text{up}}:2\\le j\\le n\\}\\cup\\{R_j^{\\text{down}}:1\\le j\\le n-1\\}\n\\]\n\ncovers every non‑diagonal cell exactly once and uses  \n\n\\[\n(n-1)+(n-1)=2n-2\n\\]\n\ntiles.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 6.  Conclusion\n\nThe lower bound \\(2n-2\\) and the explicit tiling with exactly \\(2n-2\\)\ntiles coincide.  Hence the minimum possible number of tiles is\n\n\\[\n2\\cdot2025-2=4048 .\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4048}\n\\]"
