stinct.\nApplying Lemma 1 to \\(L\\) yields\n\n\\[\n\\#\\text{rectangles covering }L\\;\\ge\\;N-1. \\tag{1}\n\\]\n\nFor the right region \\(R\\) the length of row \\(i\\) is\n\n\\[\n\\ell_i^{R}=N-p(i),\n\\]\n\nagain the set \\(\\{0,1,\\dots ,N-1\\}\\).  Exactly \\(N-1\\) rows have a positive\nright‑length, and they are distinct.  Lemma 1 applied to \\(R\\) gives\n\n\\[\n\\#\\text{rectangles covering }R\\;\\ge\\;N-1. \\tag{2}\n\\]\n\nAdding (1) and (2) we obtain the universal lower bound\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{any admissible tiling uses at least }2N-2\\text{ tiles}.}\n\\]\n\nFor \\(N=1\\) the bound gives \\(0\\) tiles, which is clearly optimal.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 5.   A tiling attaining the bound\n\nChoose the permutation  \n\n\\[\np(i)=i\\qquad(1\\le i\\le N),\n\\]\n\ni.e. the uncovered squares are the main diagonal \\((i,i)\\).\n\n*Left part.*  \nFor each column \\(c\\) with \\(1\\le c\\le N-1\\) place the vertical rectangle  \n\n\\[\nT_c^{L}=\\{(r,c):r=c+1,\\dots ,N\\},\n\\]\n\nwhich has dimensions \\((N-c)\\times1\\).  The collection\n\\(\\{T_c^{L}\\mid 1\\le c\\le N-1\\}\\) covers exactly the set \\(L\\).\n\n*Right part.*  \nFor each column \\(c\\) with \\(2\\le c\\le N\\) place the vertical rectangle  \n\n\\[\nT_c^{R}=\\{(r,c):r=1,\\dots ,c-1\\},\n\\]\n\nof dimensions \\((c-1)\\times1\\).  The rectangles\n\\(\\{T_c^{R}\\mid 2\\le c\\le N\\}\\) cover exactly the set \\(R\\).\n\nThe two families are disjoint because every square of \\(L\\) satisfies\n\\(r>c\\) while every square of \\(R\\) satisfies \\(r<c\\); the diagonal squares\n\\((i,i)\\) are uncovered by construction.  Hence we obtain a tiling of the\nboard with\n\n\\[\n(N-1)+(N-1)=2N-2\n\\]\n\ntiles.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### 6.   Conclusion\n\nThe lower bound \\(2N-2\\) holds for every admissible placement of the uncovered\nsquares, and the construction above shows that it is attainable.  Therefore\nthe minimum possible number of tiles is exactly \\(2N-2\\).\n\nFor the given board with \\(N=2025\\),\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\cdot2025-2=4048}\n\\]\n\ntiles are necessary and sufficient.  \n\n∎"
